course: dictionary
lesson: 13165
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word fortified has four meanings. «The knights rode up to the fortified town.» Strong walls and towers around a place make it fortified, so here it means protected from attack.
explain: «The cereal was fortified with iron and vitamins.» Food can be fortified too. The words cereal, iron and vitamins are about food and health, so fortified means extra goodness has been added to make the food healthier.
explain: «After a good breakfast, the runner felt fortified for the race.» Here fortified means stronger and braver. Nobody built walls, so the context shows this meaning is about feelings and strength. Always ask: does the meaning fit the words around it?
fact: Fortified has four meanings: protected by defences, with added vitamins or minerals, with strong alcohol added, or feeling stronger or braver.
fact: A fortified town has strong walls and towers to protect it from attack.
fact: Fortified food has extra vitamins or minerals added to make it healthier, like cereal fortified with iron.
fact: Fortified wine, such as port or sherry, has strong alcohol added to it.
fact: To feel fortified is to feel stronger or braver, often after food or encouragement.
exercise: «The walls of the fortified town were twenty metres high.» What does fortified mean here? | *Protected by strong walls and towers | Very quiet | Covered in bright paint | Full of vitamins
exercise: «The bread was fortified with iron and vitamins.» What does fortified mean here? | Very cold and hard | Filled with water | *Extra vitamins and minerals have been added to make it healthier | Burnt on the outside
exercise: Ben says, «I feel fortified after my breakfast.» What does he mean? | Wet through | Ready to go to sleep | *Stronger and braver | Covered in cereal
test: «The castle was fortified against the enemy army.» What does fortified mean in this sentence? | Painted bright red | Sold cheaply | Full of food | *Protected from attack
test: «The sherry was fortified.» Which meaning fits best? | Vitamins have been added | Walls have been built around it | Feeling brave | *Strong alcohol has been added
exam: «After a hard match, the team felt fortified by a bowl of porridge.» What does fortified mean here? | Covered in sugar | Sad and tired | Built with stone walls | *Stronger and ready to carry on
